## 1. Module Forge now inherits its STEM flags

[defaults.ts](src/lib/defaults.ts) gained `stemFlagsForSubject()`, a keyword classifier that sits beside the existing `SUBJECT_SUGGESTIONS` vocabulary and returns `{ isSTEM, needsEquations, needsGraphs }` plus a `StemFlags` type. It matches case-insensitively inside longer names, so "Further Maths", "Grade 11 Chemistry" and "AP Physics C" all resolve. Empty or unrecognised subjects stay neutral, and it deliberately doesn't treat biology as equations work (graphs yes, equations no) or computer science as graph work.

[modules.forge.tsx](src/routes/_authenticated/modules.forge.tsx) replaces the three hard-coded `false` values with `...stemFlags`, computed live from the Subject field, and shows a one-line hint under that field ("Maths/science subject — the module carries · LaTeX equations · graph questions") so the inheritance isn't invisible. [defaults.test.ts](src/lib/defaults.test.ts) covers the neutral cases, the maths/physics/chemistry set, biology, computer science and the substring/case matching — 6 tests.

One honest caveat: module STEM flags are currently **write-only data**. They're stored, exported and re-imported, but unlike `deck.isSTEM` (quiz/study/review keypads) and `course.isSTEM` (lesson checkpoint keypad), nothing reads `module.isSTEM` yet. So this makes the *data* correct and preserves the intent, but it won't change module screens until something consumes it.

## 2. Courses now have the module segment's LaTeX pipeline

The course segment was already ahead in breadth (DOCX export, quiz and lesson routes), so the relevant backport was the LaTeX coverage we built for modules — plus the module paper's pagination refinements, which matter directly for printing equations.

**Display** — [courses.$courseId.index.tsx](src/routes/_authenticated/courses.$courseId.index.tsx) typesets the course title, subject, description, objectives, module and lesson titles and the "Next" label; [courses.$courseId.lessons.$lessonId.tsx](src/routes/_authenticated/courses.$courseId.lessons.$lessonId.tsx) does the same for the breadcrumb, lesson title and summary, sidebar objectives, module label, block titles, image captions and the previous-lesson link; [courses.index.tsx](src/routes/_authenticated/courses.index.tsx) for card title, subject, description and next lesson. Block bodies already used a remark-math/rehype-katex renderer, and the edit route is all form inputs, so no change was needed there.

**Print** — [course-paper.tsx](src/components/print/course-paper.tsx) now typesets the table of contents rows, module and lesson headers, lesson summaries and objectives, section and assessment headers and their meta, deck headers, answer sub-headings, image captions, and every objectives list including both cover variants (title, subject, description, objectives). Answer values and explanations were already covered.

